               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\"> <defs> <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"> <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" /></marker> </defs> <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"15\" stroke=\"black\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"270\" y=\"15\" font-size=\"1em\">A</text> <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"134\" stroke=\"black\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"270\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"1em\">A</text> <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"114\" stroke=\"black\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"270\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"1em\">A</text> <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"115\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"black\" />  <line x1=\"115\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"black\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"35\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"1em\">B</text>  <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"155\" y2=\"36\" stroke=\"black\" /> <line x1=\"155\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"black\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" /> <text x=\"270\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"1em\">C</text> <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"75\" r=\"30\"></circle> <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"25\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#FF9999\"></circle><text x=\"143\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"1em\">-</text>  <circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"75\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#FF9999\"></circle><text x=\"73\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"1em\">-</text> <text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"1em\">+</text> <text x=\"140\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"1em\">+</text> <text x=\"140\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"1em\">+</text>  <text x=\"160\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"1em\">+</text> <circle cx=\"205\" cy=\"75\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#FF9999\"></circle><text x=\"202\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"1em\">-</text>  <circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"125\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#FF9999\"></circle><text x=\"143\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"1em\">-</text>  </svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Graph 1</b>: Representation of the Rutherford model.</p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "Representation of Rutherford’s atom, which features a large positive nucleus and small, negatively charged electrons around it.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### A Different Matter\n\nBesides the particles that form atoms, there was also antimatter in this period. When it meets the matter we know, the two annihilate each other — they destroy one another — forming gamma radiation (<htcite0>).\n\nThis annihilation made the early universe an extremely turbulent place. For some reason — which we are still trying to understand — an imbalance appeared as the universe cooled. As a result, we now have more matter than antimatter, although very distant regions of the universe where antimatter might still exist cannot be ruled out (<htcite1>).\n\n#### Dark Matter\n\nMatter and antimatter were not alone in the early universe. There is another kind of matter — we call it dark matter — whose composition we still do not know. We know it exists because measurements show that spiral galaxies spin faster than expected from visible matter alone (<htcite2>).\n\n#### The First Measurements\n\nThis stage of joining different particles — including the photon, the light particle —, according to our current models, lasted about 380,000 years (<htcite3>).\n\nFor this period we have no direct data to prove our theories, so we run experiments to understand what might have happened in that time.\n\nFrom 380,000 years after the Big Bang, we already have observational data — light had separated from matter. This first information from the primordial universe is called the Cosmic Microwave Background, and it is the topic of the next section of the *Atlas*.",
               "source": [
